# Build context exclusions.
#
# This file is not an optimisation. Without it the image is broken and leaks
# secrets, for three separate reasons:
#
#   1. `COPY . .` in the build stage runs *after* the deps stage's node_modules
#      is copied in. A host node_modules built on Windows or macOS therefore
#      overwrites the Alpine one — Prisma engines, esbuild and sharp all ship
#      platform-specific binaries, and the build fails or, worse, produces an
#      image that only fails at runtime.
#   2. `.env` holds real secrets. `COPY . .` bakes them into an image layer,
#      where they survive `docker run --env-file` overriding them and can be
#      read by anyone who pulls the image. Compose passes `.env.production`
#      from the host at run time; it never needs to be in the image.
#   3. The context is otherwise about 5.6 GB, nearly all of it output that no
#      layer uses.

# --- installed dependencies -------------------------------------------------
# Reinstalled for Linux in the deps stage.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- build output -----------------------------------------------------------
.next
out
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- the other apps ---------------------------------------------------------
# The server image runs the Next app and the worker. The Expo and Electron
# clients are separate artifacts that talk to it over HTTP; none of their source
# or output belongs here. apps/mobile/android alone is 1.3 GB of Gradle output
# and apps/desktop/release is 357 MB of installers.
apps

# --- local development infrastructure ---------------------------------------
# Embedded Postgres data directory and the local Memurai install. Both are large
# and one of them is a live database.
.localdb
.tools
.msitmp

# --- version control and tooling --------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- docs and container definitions -----------------------------------------
# Note: content/ is NOT excluded. The blog reads content/blog/*.mdx from disk at
# runtime, and the Dockerfile copies it deliberately.
docs
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
